---

title: "Dynamic documents as personal software (draft notes)"
date: 2026-08-20 10:00 UTC
tags:
summary: "Draft slides and speaker notes for a talk at the Recurse Center on dynamic documents as personal software: Hypercard, Margin Notes, Potluck, Embark, and current experiments at Notion."
layout: talk
main_class: wide
hidden: true

---

- talk = data.rc_talk

%article.talk
  .talk-header
    %h3.date August 2026
    %h1.title Dynamic documents as personal software
    %p.talk-context
      %strong Unlisted draft — please don't share.
      These are working slides and speaker notes for a talk I'm giving at the
      %a{href: "https://luma.com/rc-dynamic"} Recurse Center
      on Tuesday, August 25th 2026. I'm circulating this to a few people for feedback
      before the talk. Notes are pulled straight from the deck's speaker notes, so
      they're rough, uneven, and in places still a sketch.

  - slide_sizes = "(min-width: 860px) min(52vw, 815px), calc(100vw - 30px)"
  - first_slide = true
  - talk.sections.each do |section|
    - if section["title"]
      %h2.talk-section-title= section["title"]
    - section["segments"].each do |seg|
      .talk-segment
        .talk-slide
          - base = seg["slide"].sub(".webp", "")
          - srcset = "#{talk.assets}/#{base}-800.webp 800w, #{talk.assets}/#{base}-1200.webp 1200w, #{talk.assets}/#{base}.webp 1600w"
          %img{src: "#{talk.assets}/#{seg["slide"]}", srcset: srcset, sizes: slide_sizes, alt: seg["alt"], loading: first_slide ? "eager" : "lazy", fetchpriority: first_slide ? "high" : nil, decoding: "async"}
          - first_slide = false
        .talk-text
          - if seg["html"].to_s.strip.empty?
            %p.talk-no-notes No speaker notes yet.
          - else
            != seg["html"]
